      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1891 the Norfolk and Western Railroad’s Clinch Valley Extension turned Swords Creek into a bustling boomtown with hotels, a depot and blacksmith shops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/swords_creek_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Swords Creek enjoys a humid subtropical climate, with warm, humid summers and mild, wet winters typical of the Appalachians.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/swords_creek_virginia",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Two Craftsman‑style school buildings built around 1930 still line Route 634, echoing the area’s educational heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
